ability and validity of instruments measuring job satisfaction--a systematic review. Occup Med (Lond). 2003;53(3):191–200. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Cohen J Statistical Power Analysis for the Behavioral Sciences. 2nd ed. ed. Hillsdale, NJ: Erlbaum; 1988. [ Google Scholar ] 23. Sakamoto JT, Lee J, Lu DW, et al. Factors driving burnout and professional fulfillment among emergency medicine residents: A national wellness survey by the Society for Academic Emergency Medicine. AEM Educ Train. 2022;6(Suppl 1):S5–S12. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Kemper KJ, Schwartz A, Wilson PM, et al. Burnout in Pediatric Residents: Three Years of National Survey Data. Pediatrics. 2020;145(1). [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Rodriguez-Rey R, Palacios A, Alonso-Tapia J, et al. Burnout and posttraumatic stress in paediatric critical care personnel: Prediction from resilience and coping styles. Aust Crit Care. 2019;32(1):46–53. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Crowe L, Young J, Turner MJ. What is the prevalence and risk factors of burnout among pediatric intensive care staff (PICU)? A review. Transl Pediatr. 2021;10(10):2825–2835. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Jones GAL, Colville GA, Ramnarayan P, et al. Psychological impact of working in paediatric intensive care. A UK-wide prevalence study. Arch Dis Child. 2020;105(5):470–475. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Hollingsworth CE, Wesley C, Huckridge J, Finn GM, Griksaitis MJ. Impact of child death on paediatric trainees. Arch Dis Child. 2018;103(1):14–18. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Ffrench-O’Carroll R, Feeley T, Crowe S, Doherty EM. Grief reactions and coping strategies of trainee doctors working in paediatric intensive care. Br J Anaesth. 2019;123(1):74–80. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Wolfe AHJ, Hinds PS, Arnold RM, Soghier L, Tompkins R. Vulnerability of Inexperience: A Qualitative Exploration of Physic